# The language of an element: the part of the document settings that holds
# it, and the menu item that opens the settings there (ADR 0020, 0038).

languages-menu = Sprog…
# What follows from the language of a map: the words its document prints in
# words of its own, the dictionary of its spelling, the quotation marks of a mention.
languages-map-hint = For elementet og alt under det, der ikke selv siger andet. Afgør de ord, dets dokument udskriver med egne ord, såsom »Noter« og »Figur«; den ordbog, stavningen kontrolleres med; og de anførselstegn, et omtalt ord står i.
# A map that was given no language is printed in English.
languages-map-none = Ikke angivet
# Names of languages the system may have no name for, by their tags.
language-name-hbo = bibelsk hebraisk
language-name-xcl = klassisk armensk
languages-project-hint = Hvad projektet er skrevet på, for alle, det er delt med: ethvert element, der ikke får et andet, tager det. Et dokument, der hentes ind, beholder dokumentets sprog.
# Where the project chooses none, the settings' language of new texts holds; it is named.
languages-project-settings = Som i indstillingerne ({ $language })
